# Local publishing credentials — never commit
publish.local.sh

# Site identity (name, URL, author, links) — ships as site.example.yaml; copy
# to site.yaml and make it yours. Keeps a fork from inheriting someone else's
# name and URLs.
site.yaml

# Personal writing voice — ships as content_pipeline/VOICE.example.md; copy to
# content_pipeline/VOICE.md and fill in your own sample. Your VOICE.md stays local.
VOICE.md

# Working conventions for this repo (commit style, editorial habits). Personal
# preference rather than engine behaviour, so it stays local like VOICE.md -
# a fork inherits the engine, not how its author likes to work.
engine/docs/CONVENTIONS.md

# Claude-specific files (never commit any of Claude's internal files)
.claude/
claude.md
CLAUDE.md
CLAUDE.local.md

# Content pipeline working state: the ingestion queue, the drafting workspace,
# the archive of already-ingested sources, and the published Markdown. Only
# VOICE.example.md and TEMPLATE.md are tracked inside content_pipeline/.
# These patterns carry no leading slash, so they match at any depth and already
# cover content_pipeline/content/ etc. without naming the parent.
content/
drafts/
processed/
sources/
# Hand-written standalone pages (about, colophon). This author's words, same as
# the posts - the engine renders them, it doesn't ship them.
pages/
# Zine builds: generated print PDFs/.sla plus their build scripts. Personal
# output made from the author's own posts and photos, same as the rest here.
zines/

# Compiled output
public/

# Site-owned static assets: the author's own PDFs, standalone pages, and search
# engine verification files. Copied into public/ verbatim at publish time, and
# never tracked. The engine's own theme assets (style.css, search.js, the
# vendored fonts, the comment sanitizer, favicons) live in
# engine/templates/static/ and ARE tracked — that split is what lets this whole
# directory be ignored outright instead of needing a negation per theme file.
public_static/

# Runtime markers
.setup_done

# Python
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
